-- statement:
--   For an actual filtered measurable space and any finite measure on the genuine predictable time-history sigma algebra, prove that the finite Boolean set algebra generated by the original filtration's adapted initial-atom and future-half-line rectangles is measure-dense. The proof uses an independently Proved identification of that predictable sigma algebra with the generator sigma algebra and pinned MeasureDense.of_generateFrom_isSetAlgebra_finite. This provides an exact nonstochastic L² approximation foundation for indicator functions via pinned MeasureDense.indicatorConstLp_subset_closure, without assuming any stochastic isometry or Campbell identity.
